Enabled Checks:
	CLPR - There should be no combinational feedback loops. A combinational feedback loop with an odd number of inversions is an oscillator, and one with an even number of inversions is a home-made storage element. Either would create testing and verification issues.
	CONSTANT - This check ensures that a constant value does not prevent the observability of other signals.
	DANG - A signal in the design has no loads. Note that an unconnected input port within a module is also considered a dangling input.
	DCI - Report duplicate case items.
	MCA - The CASE statement must have an assignment to a variable in one of the case item blocks. The missing assignment results in an inferred latch.
	MDR - A signal should not have multiple drivers.
	MEA - The ELSE block of an IF statement must have an assignment to a variable that is assigned in the IF block. The missing assignment may result in an inferred latch.
	MEB - The IF statement must have a matching ELSE block. The missing ELSE statement could result in an inferred latch.
	MIA - The IF block of an IF statement must have an assignment to a variable. The missing assignment results in an inferred latch.
	NO_DELAY - Designs should not contain delay statements. The check reports the use of delay statements.
	NO_INITIAL - Designs should not have initial statements. The check reports the use of initial statements.
	NOT_SYNTHESIZABLE - Report constructs that may not be synthesizable or may be partially synthesizable. Synthesis tools may differ on what they can synthesize.
	PREV_ASSIGN - Report situation where an assignment may overwrite a previous assignment.
	RRW - A read-write race condition may exist when the same variable can potentially be read from and written to in different always/initial blocks.
	RSTASR - Report flip-flops that have both an asynchronous set and reset.
	RSTS - Synchronous preset/clear must be used.
	UBA - There should be no signals referenced before they are assigned within a non-sequential block. The check reports such signals. There is an option to also report signals that are referenced before they are assigned in sequential blocks.
	UND - A signal is not driven.
	UNI - Input pin of an primitive gate is not connected.
	UNO - Output port of a module must be connected.
	UNR - A bit-select or part-select of a net is not driven.
	NO_SYNCH_DEASSERT_RST - Report on the reset signals not synchronously deasserted.
	UNCONNECTED_UNDRIVEN_USED_NET - Report signals that are used but which trace back to a floating node.
	UNCONNECTED_UNDRIVEN_USED_PIN - Report hierarchical instance pins that are unconnected but used internal to the instance.
	LATCH_CREATED - Report on every latch created or inferred.
